  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{8}z\\,dy]dA\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}z\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{D}z[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=8}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3})[{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3}){[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=4}\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{[8x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =8(16-4) \\\\  & =96\\end{aligned}\n$$",
